From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] api: add rooted native value construction and string
 reuse

Snapshot own enumerable entries and descriptors without constructing
JavaScript pair arrays or descriptor objects. Preserve key order,
getter/proxy effects, SameValue comparisons and mutation detection.

Construct objects and dense arrays directly into rooted storage through
ordered callbacks. Reuse bounded runtime-owned immutable layouts, with
key-content collision checks, individual LRU eviction and non-owning
layout hints. Indexed or duplicate keys and mutable dictionary layouts
retain ordinary property definitions. Templates hold no document values.

Borrow already-rooted values across native callbacks and reuse eligible
UTF-8 conversions in an invocation-owned scope. Nested scopes restore
their predecessor and retain bounded actual string backing storage;
returned conversion results remain independently owned.

Expose the Static Hermes UTF-8 writer and permit Hermes values as native
arguments. Keep FFI, layout, callback collection, descriptor and string
lifetime coverage with these interfaces.
